Table full name: HTAN_2.HTAN.CLINICAL_TIER1_DIAGNOSIS_CURRENT
Column name: Gleason_Grade_Tertiary Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the tertiary pattern as described by the Gleason Grading System.
Column name: Method_of_Diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: Text term used to describe the method used to confirm the patients malignant diagnosis.
Column name: Ovarian_Specimen_Status Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the physical condition of the involved ovary.
Column name: Best_Overall_Response Type: TEXT Description: The best improvement achieved throughout the entire course of protocol treatment.
Column name: Year_of_Diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: Numeric value to represent the year of an individual's initial pathologic diagnosis of cancer.
Column name: INSS_Stage Type: TEXT Description: Text term used to describe the staging classification of neuroblastic tumors, as defined by the International Neuroblastoma Staging System (INSS).
Column name: Anaplasia_Present_Type Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the morphologic findings indicating the presence of a malignant cellular infiltrate characterized by the presence of large pleomorphic cells, necrosis, and high mitotic activity in a tissue sample.
Column name: AJCC_Clinical_Stage Type: TEXT Description: Stage group determined from clinical information on the tumor (T), regional node (N) and metastases (M) and by grouping cases with similar prognosis for cancer.
Column name: AJCC_Clinical_T Type: TEXT Description: Extent of the primary cancer based on evidence obtained from clinical assessment parameters determined prior to treatment.
Column name: Morphology Type: TEXT Description: The third edition of the International Classification of Diseases for Oncology, published in 2000 used principally in tumor and cancer registries for coding the site (topography) and the histology (morphology) of neoplasms. The study of the structure of the cells and their arrangement to constitute tissues and, finally, the association among these to form organs. In pathology, the microscopic process of identifying normal and abnormal morphologic characteristics in tissues, by employing various cytochemical and immunocytochemical stains. A system of numbered categories for representation of data.
Column name: INPC_Histologic_Group Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the classification of neuroblastomas distinguishing between favorable and unfavorable histologic groups. The histologic score, defined by the International Neuroblastoma Pathology Classification (INPC), is based on age, mitosis-karyorrhexis index (MKI), stromal content and degree of tumor cell differentiation.
Column name: Cog_Neuroblastoma_Risk_Group Type: TEXT Description: Text term that represents the categorization of patients on the basis of prognostic factors per a system developed by Children's Oncology Group (COG). Risk level is used to assign treatment intensity.
Column name: Gleason_Grade_Group Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the overall grouping of grades defined by the Gleason grading classification, which is used to determine the aggressiveness of prostate cancer. Note that this grade describes the entire prostatectomy specimen and is not specific to the sample used for sequencing.
Column name: Synchronous_Malignancy Type: TEXT Description: A yes/no/unknown indicator used to describe whether the patient had an additional malignant diagnosis at the same time the tumor used for sequencing was diagnosed. If both tumors were sequenced, both tumors would have synchronous malignancies.
Column name: Vascular_Invasion_Type Type: TEXT Description: Text term that represents the type of vascular tumor invasion.
Column name: Tumor_Grade Type: TEXT Description: Numeric value to express the degree of abnormality of cancer cells, a measure of differentiation and aggressiveness.
Column name: HTAN_Participant_ID Type: TEXT Description: HTAN ID associated with a patient based on HTAN ID SOP (eg HTANx_yyy )
Column name: IGCCCG_Stage Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the International Germ Cell Cancer Collaborative Group (IGCCCG), a grouping used to further classify metastatic testicular tumors.
Column name: Gross_Tumor_Weight Type: TEXT Description: Numeric value used to describe the gross pathologic tumor weight, measured in grams.
Column name: Id Type: TEXT Description: Unique identifier of entity e.g. a96059eb-81af-4b24-ae50-9242c0d8f819
Column name: AJCC_Clinical_N Type: TEXT Description: Extent of the regional lymph node involvement for the cancer based on evidence obtained from clinical assessment parameters determined prior to treatment.
Column name: Mitosis_Karyorrhexis_Index Type: TEXT Description: Text term that represents the component of the International Neuroblastoma Pathology Classification (INPC) for mitosis-karyorrhexis index (MKI).
Column name: AJCC_Pathologic_M Type: TEXT Description: Code to represent the defined absence or presence of distant spread or metastases (M) to locations via vascular channels or lymphatics beyond the regional lymph nodes, using criteria established by the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC).
Column name: IRS_Stage Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the classification of rhabdomyosarcoma tumors, as defined by the Intergroup Rhabdomyosarcoma Study (IRS).
Column name: Tissue_or_Organ_of_Origin Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the anatomic site of origin, of the patient's malignant disease, as described by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O).
Column name: Perineural_Invasion_Present Type: TEXT Description: A yes/no indicator to ask if perineural invasion or infiltration of tumor or cancer is present.
Column name: Medulloblastoma_Molecular_Classification Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the classification of medulloblastoma tumors based on molecular features.
Column name: Lymph_Nodes_Positive Type: TEXT Description: The number of lymph nodes involved with disease as determined by pathologic examination.
Column name: Breslow_Thickness Type: TEXT Description: The number that describes the distance, in millimeters, between the upper layer of the epidermis and the deepest point of tumor penetration.
Column name: Anaplasia_Present Type: TEXT Description: Yes/no/unknown/Not Reported indicator used to describe whether anaplasia was present at the time of diagnosis.
Column name: AJCC_Clinical_M Type: TEXT Description: Extent of the distant metastasis for the cancer based on evidence obtained from clinical assessment parameters determined prior to treatment.
Column name: HTAN_Center Type: TEXT Description: Name of HTAN Center e.g. HTAN HTAPP
Column name: Metastasis_at_Diagnosis_Site Type: TEXT Description: Text term to identify an anatomic site in which metastatic disease involvement is found.
Column name: Margins_Involved_Site Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the anatomic sites that were involved in the survival margins.
Column name: Progression_or_Recurrence Type: TEXT Description: Yes/No/unknown indicator to identify whether a patient has had a new tumor event after initial treatment.
Column name: WHO_CNS_Grade Type: TEXT Description: WHO CNS Grade
Column name: Days_to_Recurrence Type: TEXT Description: Number of days between the date used for index and the date the patient's disease recurred. If not applicable please enter 'Not Applicable'
Column name: entityId Type: TEXT Description: Synapse ID of entity
Column name: Pregnant_at_Diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to indicate whether the patient was pregnant at the time they were diagnosed.
Column name: Vascular_Invasion_Present Type: TEXT Description: The yes/no indicator to ask if large vessel or venous invasion was detected by surgery or presence in a tumor specimen.
Column name: IRS_Group Type: TEXT Description: Text term used to describe the classification of rhabdomyosarcoma tumors, as defined by the Intergroup Rhabdomyosarcoma Study (IRS).
Column name: Greatest_Tumor_Dimension Type: TEXT Description: Numeric value that represents the measurement of the widest portion of the tumor in centimeters.
Column name: Days_to_Progression_Free Type: TEXT Description: Number of days between the date used for index and the date the patient's disease was formally confirmed as progression-free. If not applicable please enter 'Not Applicable'
Column name: Micropapillary_Features Type: TEXT Description: The yes/no/unknown indicator used to describe whether micropapillary features were determined to be present.
Column name: Tumor_Confined_to_Organ_of_Origin Type: TEXT Description: The yes/no/unknown indicator used to describe whether the tumor is confined to the organ where it originated and did not spread to a proximal or distant location within the body.
Column name: Lymph_Nodes_Tested Type: TEXT Description: The number of lymph nodes tested to determine whether lymph nodes were involved with disease as determined by a pathologic examination.
Column name: Non_Nodal_Regional_Disease Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe whether the patient had non-nodal regional disease.
Column name: Component Type: TEXT Description: Category of metadata (e.g. Diagnosis, Biospecimen, scRNA-seq Level 1, etc.); provide the same one for all items/rows.
Column name: Ovarian_Surface_Involvement Type: TEXT Description: The text term that describes whether the surface tissue (outer boundary) of the ovary shows evidence of involvement or presence of cancer.
Column name: Precancerous_Condition_Type Type: TEXT Description: The classification of pre-cancerous cells found in a specific collection of data being studied by the Consortium for Molecular and Cellular Characterization of Screen-Detected Lesions (MCL).
Column name: Manifest_Version Type: NUMBER Description: Latest version of metadata manifest
Column name: Days_to_Last_Follow_up Type: TEXT Description: Time interval from the date of last follow up to the date of initial pathologic diagnosis, represented as a calculated number of days. If not applicable please enter 'Not Applicable'
Column name: AJCC_Pathologic_Stage Type: TEXT Description: The extent of a cancer, especially whether the disease has spread from the original site to other parts of the body based on AJCC staging criteria.
Column name: Site_of_Resection_or_Biopsy Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the anatomic site of the resection or biopsy of the patient's malignant disease, as described by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O).
Column name: Cog_Rhabdomyosarcoma_Risk_Group Type: TEXT Description: Text term used to describe the classification of rhabdomyosarcoma, as defined by the Children's Oncology Group (COG).
Column name: Progression_or_Recurrence_Type Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the type of progressive or recurrent disease or relapsed disease.
Column name: Gleason_Patterns_Percent Type: TEXT Description: Numeric value that represents the percentage of Patterns 4 and 5, which is used when the Gleason score is greater than 7 to predict prognosis.
Column name: Primary_Gleason_Grade Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the primary Gleason score, which describes the pattern of cells making up the largest area of the tumor. The primary and secondary Gleason pattern grades are combined to determine the patient's Gleason grade group, which is used to determine the aggresiveness of prostate cancer. Note that this grade describes the entire prostatectomy specimen and is not specific to the sample used for sequencing.
Column name: Manifest_Id Type: TEXT Description: Synapse ID of manifest containing file annotation
Column name: Tumor_Focality Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe whether the patient's disease originated in a single location or multiple locations.
Column name: Residual_Disease Type: TEXT Description: Text terms to describe the status of a tissue margin following surgical resection.
Column name: Metastasis_at_Diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the extent of metastatic disease present at diagnosis.
Column name: Lymph_Node_Involved_Site Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the anatomic site of lymph node involvement.
Column name: Days_to_Last_Known_Disease_Status Type: TEXT Description: Time interval from the date of last follow up to the date of initial pathologic diagnosis, represented as a calculated number of days. If not applicable please enter 'Not Applicable'
Column name: Prior_Treatment Type: TEXT Description: A yes/no/unknown/not applicable indicator related to the administration of therapeutic agents received before the body specimen was collected.
Column name: Supratentorial_Localization Type: TEXT Description: Text term to specify the location of the supratentorial tumor.
Column name: Prior_Malignancy Type: TEXT Description: The yes/no/unknown indicator used to describe the patient's history of prior cancer diagnosis.
Column name: Secondary_Gleason_Grade Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the secondary Gleason score, which describes the pattern of cells making up the second largest area of the tumor. The primary and secondary Gleason pattern grades are combined to determine the patient's Gleason grade group, which is used to determine the aggresiveness of prostate cancer. Note that this grade describes the entire prostatectomy specimen and is not specific to the sample used for sequencing.
Column name: Classification_of_Tumor Type: TEXT Description: Text that describes the kind of disease present in the tumor specimen as related to a specific timepoint.
Column name: Age_at_Diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: Age at the time of diagnosis expressed in number of days since birth.
Column name: Primary_Diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: Text term used to describe the patient's histologic diagnosis, as described by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O).
Column name: INPC_Grade Type: TEXT Description: Text term used to describe the classification of neuroblastic differentiation within neuroblastoma tumors, as defined by the International Neuroblastoma Pathology Classification (INPC).
Column name: Days_to_Progression Type: TEXT Description: Number of days between the date used for index and the date the patient's disease progressed. If not applicable please enter 'Not Applicable'
Column name: Mitotic_Count Type: TEXT Description: The number of mitoses identified under the microscope in tumors. The method of counting varies, according to the specific tumor examined. Usually, the mitotic count is determined based on the number of mitoses per high power field (40X) or 10 high power fields.
Column name: AJCC_Pathologic_N Type: TEXT Description: The codes that represent the stage of cancer based on the nodes present (N stage) according to criteria based on multiple editions of the AJCC's Cancer Staging Manual.
Column name: Progression_or_Recurrence_Anatomic_Site Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the anatomic site of resection; biopsy; tissue or organ of biospecimen origin; progression or recurrent disease; treatment
Column name: Percent_Tumor_Invasion Type: TEXT Description: The percentage of tumor cells spread locally in a malignant neoplasm through infiltration or destruction of adjacent tissue.
Column name: Last_Known_Disease_Status Type: TEXT Description: Text term that describes the last known state or condition of an individual's neoplasm.
Column name: Days_to_Diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: Number of days between the date used for index and the date the patient was diagnosed with the malignant disease. If not applicable please enter 'Not Applicable'
Column name: International_Prognostic_Index Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the International Prognostic Index, which classifies the prognosis of patients with aggressive non-Hodgkin's lymphoma.
Column name: Laterality Type: TEXT Description: For tumors in paired organs, designates the side on which the cancer originates.
Column name: AJCC_Pathologic_T Type: TEXT Description: Code of pathological T (primary tumor) to define the size or contiguous extension of the primary tumor (T), using staging criteria from the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC).
Column name: ISS_Stage Type: TEXT Description: The multiple myeloma disease stage at diagnosis.
Column name: AJCC_Staging_System_Edition Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the version or edition of the American Joint Committee on Cancer Staging Handbooks, a publication by the group formed for the purpose of developing a system of staging for cancer that is acceptable to the American medical profession and is compatible with other accepted classifications.
Column name: INRG_Stage Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the staging classification of neuroblastic tumors, as defined by the International Neuroblastoma Risk Group (INRG).
Column name: Peritoneal_Fluid_Cytological_Status Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the malignant status of the peritoneal fluid determined by cytologic testing.
Column name: First_Symptom_Prior_to_Diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: Text term used to describe the patient's first symptom experienced prior to diagnosis and thought to be related to the disease.
Column name: Non_Nodal_Tumor_Deposits Type: TEXT Description: The yes/no/unknown indicator used to describe the presence of tumor deposits in the pericolic or perirectal fat or in adjacent mesentery away from the leading edge of the tumor.
Column name: WHO_NTE_Grade Type: TEXT Description: WHO NTE Grade
Column name: Tumor_Largest_Dimension_Diameter Type: TEXT Description: Numeric value used to describe the maximum diameter or dimension of the primary tumor, measured in centimeters.
Column name: Lymphatic_Invasion_Present Type: TEXT Description: A yes/no indicator to ask if small or thin-walled vessel invasion is present, indicating lymphatic involvement
Column name: Tumor_Depth Type: TEXT Description: Numeric value that represents the depth of tumor invasion, measured in millimeters (mm).
Column name: Margin_Distance Type: TEXT Description: Numeric value (in centimeters) that represents the distance between the tumor and the surgical margin.
