The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'HTAN_2': {'HTAN': ['SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT', 'CLINICAL_TIER1_DIAGNOSIS_CURRENT']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below are the columns that appear most relevant to the problem and how they can be used.

• "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID": to identify the 74‑year‑old human stage  
• "SEX": to separate female vs male cells  
• "CELL_TYPE_COARSE": to keep only epithelial cells  
• "CLUSTERS": to focus on cluster 41  
• "FEATURE_NAME": the gene symbol  
• "X_VALUE": continuous gene‑expression value we must average and compare  
• "HTAN_PARTICIPANT_ID" (and/or "DONOR_ID"): possible join key to the clinical table if age information were needed from that table

Conditions we will likely employ

• "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'  
• "CLUSTERS" = '41'  
• "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID" = (value that corresponds to “74‑year‑old human stage”; we will discover it with exploratory queries)  
• "SEX" IN ('Female','Male')  — spellings verified with DISTINCT queries  

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Ten step‑wise Snowflake SQL queries (each capped with LIMIT 20) that explore the data and finally compute the requested 20‑gene list.  Every identifier is double‑quoted, every query is in its own ```sql``` block, and a brief description precedes each.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at distinct cluster labels.
SELECT DISTINCT "CLUSTERS"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Check distinct values recorded in the SEX column.
SELECT DISTINCT "SEX"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) List all distinct human‑stage ontology IDs to locate the 74‑year‑old term.
SELECT DISTINCT "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID" ILIKE '%HsapDv:%'
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Inspect examples of epithelial cells in cluster 41.
SELECT *
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Show average expression (X_VALUE) per SEX for a single gene (e.g., EPCAM) in the target group.
SELECT "SEX",
       AVG("X_VALUE") AS "avg_xvalue_epcam"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "FEATURE_NAME" = 'EPCAM'
  AND "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID" = 'HsapDv:0000xxx'   --‑‑replace with 74‑yo code
GROUP BY "SEX"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Same as #5 but averaged for every gene; no difference computed yet.
SELECT "FEATURE_NAME",
       "SEX",
       AVG("X_VALUE") AS "avg_xvalue"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID" = 'HsapDv:0000xxx'   --replace
GROUP BY "FEATURE_NAME", "SEX"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Compute female minus male average X_VALUE for each gene via conditional aggregation.
SELECT
  "FEATURE_NAME",
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_female",
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_male",
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END)
  - AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "female_minus_male"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID" = 'HsapDv:0000xxx'   --replace
GROUP BY "FEATURE_NAME"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Same as #7 but keep only genes measured in ≥100 cells (example threshold) to stabilize estimates.
SELECT
  "FEATURE_NAME",
  COUNT(*)                                AS "cell_count",
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_female",
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_male",
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END)
  - AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "female_minus_male"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID" = 'HsapDv:0000xxx'   --replace
GROUP BY "FEATURE_NAME"
HAVING "cell_count" >= 100
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Rank genes by the absolute female‑minus‑male difference (largest first).
SELECT
  "FEATURE_NAME",
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_female",
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "avg_male",
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END)
  - AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END) AS "female_minus_male"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."SCRNASEQ_MSK_SCLC_COMBINED_SAMPLES_CURRENT"
WHERE "CELL_TYPE_COARSE" = 'Epithelial'
  AND "CLUSTERS" = '41'
  AND "DEVELOPMENT_STAGE_ONTOLOGY_TERM_ID" = 'HsapDv:0000xxx'   --replace
GROUP BY "FEATURE_NAME"
ORDER BY ABS(
  AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Female' THEN "X_VALUE" END)
  - AVG(CASE WHEN "SEX" = 'Male'   THEN "X_VALUE" END)
) DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

